#: ../../../project-security/verifying-signatures.rst:329
#: 99ff0895e1eb4121be80d13c4adc4dd5
msgid ""
"Every Qubes ISO is released with a **detached PGP signature** file, which "
"you can find on the `downloads <https://www.qubes-os.org/downloads/>`__ page "
"alongside the ISO. If the filename of your ISO is :file:`Qubes-"
"R{X}-86_64.iso`, then the name of the signature file for that ISO "
"is :file:`Qubes-R{X}-86_64.iso.asc`, where :samp:`{X}` is a specific release "
"of Qubes. The signature filename is always the same as the ISO filename "
"followed by ``.asc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../project-security/verifying-signatures.rst:331
#: 5044fc575ec5424494e77c27d3a13a58
msgid ""
"**Download both the ISO and its signature file**. Put both of them **in the "
"same directory**, then navigate to that directory. Now, you can verify the "
"ISO by executing this GPG command in the directory that contains both files, "
"make sure to replace :samp:`Qubes-R{X}` by the correct release number "
"(i.e.: :samp:`Qubes-R{4.3}`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../project-security/verifying-signatures.rst:344
#: 9083dc3665a64484a3cee69e5e6802f9
msgid ""
"This is just an example, so the output you receive will not look exactly the "
"same. What matters is the line that says ``Good signature from \"Qubes OS "
"Release X Signing Key\"``. This confirms that the signature on the ISO is "
"good."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../project-security/verifying-signatures.rst:346
#: 8986c53e4e0a4bf99e7a54071d313d82
